      "problem": "Given that $g^2 -18g + 81 = 0$, what are the values of $g?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{2}-18g+81 & =0 \\\\ {g}^{2}-2\\cdot 9\\cdot g+{9}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (g-9)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(g-9)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |g-9| & =0 \\\\ g-9 & =0 \\\\ g & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
